# Tenant currency (Settings SSOT)

Money display and cost math labels must follow the **tenant currency setting**, same class as language — not a hardcoded `EUR`, `USD`, or `€`.

## SSOT

| Layer | Source |
|---|---|
| Persistence | `app_settings` key `locale.currency_code` (tenant scope, Localization category) |
| Seed default | `src-tauri/src/db/seeder.rs` → `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` |
| Runtime store | `useLocaleStore().activeCurrencyCode` (`src/stores/locale-store.ts`) |
| Shared constants | `src/lib/currency.ts` (`FALLBACK_CURRENCY_CODE`, option list, normalize) |
| UI formatting | `useFormatters().formatCurrency(amount)` only |

Settings UI: `SettingsValueEditor` select for `locale.currency_code` (live-updates the store on save).

## Required path (every module)

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
const { formatCurrency } = useFormatters();
<span>{formatCurrency(line.cost)}</span>

// ❌ BAD — hardcodes product currency
formatCurrency(line.cost, "EUR")
`${amount.toFixed(2)} €`
<span>€{amount}</span>
```

- Prefer the hook with **no** currency override for normal tenant amounts.
- Pass an override **only** for true multi-currency surfaces (e.g. FX source currency) where the amount’s currency is not the tenant base.
- Pure `formatCurrency(value, locale, currency)` in `src/utils/formatters.ts` **requires** an explicit ISO 4217 code — do not reintroduce a default of `"EUR"`.
- Backend/storage may keep amounts as plain numbers; display currency is a presentation concern unless a domain table already stores `currency_code` (Finance / inventory valuation). Do not invent a second parallel “display currency” setting.

## Extending the currency list

1. Add the ISO 4217 code to `CURRENCY_CODE_OPTIONS` in `src/lib/currency.ts`.
2. Add `options.currency.<CODE>` in `en` / `fr` `settings.json`.
3. Do not hardcode the new code in feature modules.

## Anti-patterns

- Defaulting formatters or IPC DTOs to `"EUR"` / `"USD"`.
- Module-local currency symbols or `Intl.NumberFormat({ style: "currency", currency: "EUR" })`.
- Coupling currency to language (`fr` ⇒ EUR, `en` ⇒ USD). Language and currency are independent Settings.

```text
❌ BAD — labor/planning/WO costs always show €
✅ GOOD — Settings → Localization → Currency drives all formatCurrency() output
```
